{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1467139-pugmire-pitbulls-as-companions","id":1467139,"title":"(Pugmire) Pitbulls as Companions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-07T18:43:32-08:00","id":1467139,"title":"(Pugmire) Pitbulls as Companions","content":"So I'm running a Pugmire game and I decided to list Pitbulls as companions. What you guys think? I meet a pitbull they are just... sociable as all get out the poor things being stereotyped to be feral only just terrible...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27163-crimson_fairy","name":"Crimson_Fairy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T10:57:38-08:00","id":1467179,"title":"","content":"While I appreciate the intent, and Eddy's been very clear about not letting real world breed stereotypes override what people playing the game want to assign here, I think it's worth considering your logic before opting for this.<br /> <br /> There's no such thing as &quot;unsociable&quot; breeds. Dogs are social animals that have been bred for thousands of years by another social animal to form a tight cross-species bond. All dogs, just like all humans, have some social drive regardless of their individual personality and other emotional needs.<br /> <br /> Getting too wrapped up in the idea that &quot;Companion = social dog,&quot; would just mean all dogs are Companions. <br /> <br /> If you want to break the stereotype, Fettle seems a good choice to represent the physicality of pitbulls without getting into how they're viewed by humans now. If you want to subvert their stereotypes by showing how what so many people think poorly about pitbulls is really what makes them Good Dogs, Worker seems a good choice. Look at the Breed Tricks. How many of those are things you can say, &quot;OK, I can totally see a pitbull doing that,&quot; since that's one of the big mechanical impacts of Breed selection.<br /> <br /> You can still start with a 15 or 14 in Charisma and play a lovable friendly dog regardless of what mechanical Breed you pick.<br /> <br /> So, obviously, it wouldn't be my first choice because I think it undermines what makes Companions special a bit, and I don't think really does pitbulls justice on celebrating what they were bred to be good at to instead focus too much of not falling into the stereotypes people have about them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T11:36:14-08:00","id":1467188,"title":"","content":"Well I seen pitbulls and they are imo when taken care of tend to be one of the more adorkable breeds imo","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27163-crimson_fairy","name":"Crimson_Fairy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T13:07:43-08:00","id":1467194,"title":"","content":"My take is more that it doesn't really matter what breed a dog is when determining their Breed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T23:33:19-08:00","id":1467235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crimson_Fairy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1467139-pugmire-pitbulls-as-companions?p=1467188#post1467188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I seen pitbulls and they are imo when taken care of tend to be one of the more adorkable breeds imo</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the exact mentality I think you shouldn't go for.<br /> <br /> Every time I've run or played with the core sample PCs, Spike is the most adorkable dog, even across four different players. He's just a big lovable idiot that means well and tries hard and everyone plays him as a goof. Yasha is more socially adept as a Companion though. Not because she isn't adorable in her own way, but she's got a natural capacity to get people to go along with her because of her earnest-to-the-point-of-naive nature. <br /> <br /> That's why my suggestion is to really look at what the mechanics of the Breeds are.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T01:12:32-08:00","id":1467243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1467139-pugmire-pitbulls-as-companions?p=1467235#post1467235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the exact mentality I think you shouldn't go for.<br /> <br /> Every time I've run or played with the core sample PCs, Spike is the most adorkable dog, even across four different players. He's just a big lovable idiot that means well and tries hard and everyone plays him as a goof. Yasha is more socially adept as a Companion though. Not because she isn't adorable in her own way, but she's got a natural capacity to get people to go along with her because of her earnest-to-the-point-of-naive nature.<br /> <br /> That's why my suggestion is to really look at what the mechanics of the Breeds are.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There also the fact I never heard of most dog breeds in the book so just named one which I rationalized to fit the theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27163-crimson_fairy","name":"Crimson_Fairy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T06:59:29-08:00","id":1467257,"title":"","content":"While I think you should do whatever you feel is most fun for your game, but the book already contains a breed for pit bulls. The Staffordshire bull terrier is one of the breeds that can be known as a pit bull and one of the families under the Pointers breed is Staffordshire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11274-tamind01","name":"Tamind01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T10:31:22-08:00","id":1467268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crimson_Fairy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1467139-pugmire-pitbulls-as-companions?p=1467243#post1467243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There also the fact I never heard of most dog breeds in the book so just named one which I rationalized to fit the theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK... but my point isn't about the example breeds listed in the book under each Breed. It's about making sure the mechanics tied to Breed work for how you and your players envision the breed in question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tamind01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1467139-pugmire-pitbulls-as-companions?p=1467257#post1467257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Staffordshire bull terrier is one of the breeds that can be known as a pit bull and one of the families under the Pointers breed is Staffordshire.</div> </div> </div> </div>This... isn't the best way to approach things. There are a few examples of closely related breeds that are in different Breeds in the book. Wolfhounds are Runners despite their likely lineage as a cross between mastiffs (Fettles) and sigh-hounds (split between Pointers and Runners). Eddy's been very clear he doesn't want the game to be bogged down in citing real world breed standards, and that Breed is about themes and archetypes to build off of.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T05:56:48-08:00","id":1467343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crimson_Fairy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1467139-pugmire-pitbulls-as-companions#post1467139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm running a Pugmire game and I decided to list Pitbulls as companions. What you guys think? I meet a pitbull they are just... sociable as all get out the poor things being stereotyped to be feral only just terrible...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If that's how you want to work Pibbles in your game, go for it!<br /> <br /> That said, one thing that maybe isn't clear in the book is that Breed is really shorthand for <i>upbringing</i>, not any kind of &quot;racial class.&quot; I defaulted to how humans perceive and categorize them for easier understanding, but really how a dog is trained matters more, and that's what Breed is meant to represent. (I did have some optional rules for &quot;breed tendencies&quot; in the Early Access book, but I cut them for the final product, and it's something I've been moving away from since then.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T06:27:02-08:00","id":1467350,"title":"","content":"Ah okay well I wanted to name a 'last name' and I hardly know many dog breeds well by name and decided a pitbull be a good Companion 'name' cuz their so sweet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27163-crimson_fairy","name":"Crimson_Fairy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}